# Student-subject concentration across domains — final report

## 0. Data provenance and unit of analysis
- File: `data/meta-regression_study_data_heterogeneity_in_replication_projects.csv` — 927 rows x 58 columns, 141 unique O/R ids, 135 unique original-study titles.
- Many Labs entries repeat one original study across labs (`lab_id`); therefore the analysis unit is the **unique original study (title)**, not the data row.
- Approved rules: discipline grouping; title dedup; `subjects.o` = unique value within title (verified 0 conflicts); `subjects.r` = ANY rule (13 titles have conflicting `subjects.r`); no exclusion of `drop`/`aggregated`; missing subjects (rpp.154) kept in denominator as non-students.
- Integrity check: titles with >1 distinct `subjects.o` = 0; titles with >1 distinct `subjects.r` = 13 (these need the ANY rule).
- Rows with missing subjects type (literal `n/a` in the file): 1 -> rpp.154 (rpp, discipline=Social, drop=True) -> kept in the denominator and counted as NOT students.

